    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Inception Mercury is an API only, text in and text out line with two versions, both supporting reasoning and neither publishing open weights. Context windows run from 128000 to 260000 tokens, and maximum output runs from 50000 to 65536 tokens, so long documents and long answers are both workable. The newer Mercury 2.5 is far cheaper, at $0.04 per million input and $0.15 output, against $0.25 and $0.75 for Mercury 2, and it also carries the larger context window. The facts suggest the family suits text reasoning tasks where a large context and a low price matter, such as summarising or analysing long documents. Limits are the text only input and output, the absence of open weights, and the fact that pricing and capability differ sharply between the two versions, so the older one is the costly choice.",
